From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 14:50:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] generic plugin scheduler dispatch (GriefPrevention,
 Shopkeepers)

Refactors the GriefPrevention-specific dispatch into LophinyaPluginSchedulerDispatch,
a generic SHA-256-keyed rule table: {className, strategy, playerField} entries,
one list per exact plugin jar version. Adding a future plugin's dispatch becomes a
declarative rule entry after its own callsite research, not a bespoke Java class -
the mechanical wiring is now shared, the per-plugin verification step is not (and
should never be) removed.

Three strategies cover everything found so far: GLOBAL (no single player/location
context), GLOBAL_OR_PLAYER_FIELD (two variants of one class distinguished by a
reflected Player field's nullness), PLAYER_FIELD (always a single known player).
Repeat-vs-one-shot is derived generically from the task's period rather than
hardcoded per rule.

Rule set 1 - GriefPrevention 16.18.7, 4 classes, unchanged.

Rule set 2 - Shopkeepers 2.27.0, 5 classes. These are exactly the five sync
scheduler registrations that abort SKShopkeepersPlugin.onEnable() on stock Folia,
found one at a time by re-running an isolated DevServer cold start after each rule
and taking whatever the next runtime blocker turned out to be:

  EntityAI$TickTask                              (EntityAI.java:383,      timer 3/3)
  CitizensShops$DelayedSetupTask                 (CitizensShops.java:183, later 3)
  ShopkeeperSpawnQueue$SpawnerTask               (TaskQueue.java:191,     timer 1/3)
  ShopkeeperSpawner$CheckUnspawnableShopkeepersTask
                                                 (ShopkeeperSpawner:99,   later 5)
  ShopkeeperTicker$ShopkeeperTickTask            (ShopkeeperTicker:229,   timer 5/5)

All five are named classes (not lambdas) and all five are whole-server scans or
heartbeats with no single player/location context, so GLOBAL is the only honest
target. Each one keeps its loop intact on one thread - nothing here fans a loop out
per region, so the shared-static and batched-dirty-flag assumptions those loops make
are exactly as valid as they are on Paper today.

What this does NOT claim: Shopkeepers' entity shops do not work. Spawning happens
from the global region, which owns no world chunks, so every spawn is rejected by
the ownership check. onEnable() completing means commands and ~96 event handlers
register - it is a C-BIN/C-SCHED result, not a working plugin. T-12's finding that
EntityAI cannot be made correct across regions stands untouched.

Deliberately NOT added: WorldSaveDespawner$RespawnShopkeepersAfterWorldSaveTask.
Its scheduling call runs BEFORE despawnShopkeepersInWorld (WorldSaveDespawner.java:
80-95), so letting it through would turn today's clean no-op (nothing despawned,
nothing pending) into shopkeepers marked PENDING_WORLD_SAVE_RESPAWN with a respawn
that cannot succeed. Rejecting it is the safer state.

Kill switch: -Dlophinya.compat.pluginSchedulerDispatch=true (default off).

diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
index 1b54ac91e6a34dbc51fa4ccacd7934fc0c85c1c5..5eb4529dbc3057bb0a98a333a989ad98833992da 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
@@ -274,6 +274,15 @@ class PaperPluginInstanceManager {
         }
         // Lophinya end - restored async scheduler: cancel Bukkit tasks on disable, like Paper does
 
+        // Lophinya start - generic plugin scheduler redispatch: cancel any tasks this plugin had
+        // redispatched via LophinyaPluginSchedulerDispatch, same reasoning as the block above -
+        // otherwise a disabled plugin's redispatched tasks would keep running forever.
+        try {
+            fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaPluginSchedulerDispatch.cancelAll(plugin);
+        } catch (Throwable ignored) {
+        }
+        // Lophinya end - generic plugin scheduler redispatch
+
         // Paper start - Folia schedulers
         try {
             this.server.getGlobalRegionScheduler().cancelTasks(plugin);
diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
index f5d23194f7c6d7c9de3b01c396ca8df9816833d8..0e3c35e294e31e24ba260dbbf3eb5d8904ca0ddd 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
@@ -550,6 +550,16 @@ public class CraftScheduler implements BukkitScheduler {
             this.addTask(task);
             return task;
         }
+        // Lophinya start - generic plugin scheduler redispatch (opt-in, see
+        // LophinyaPluginSchedulerDispatch for scope and rationale). Only reached for sync tasks on
+        // the main (non-async) scheduler - exactly the case stock Folia has no home for.
+        if (!this.isAsyncScheduler && task.isSync()) {
+            final CraftTask redispatched = fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaPluginSchedulerDispatch.tryDispatch(task, delay, task.getPeriod());
+            if (redispatched != null) {
+                return redispatched;
+            }
+        }
+        // Lophinya end - generic plugin scheduler redispatch
         throw new UnsupportedOperationException(fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaSchedulerDiagnostics.reportRejected(
             task.getOwner(), delay, task.getPeriod(), !task.isSync()));
         // Lophinya end - restore Bukkit async scheduler semantics + diagnostic guard
